figcraft (embedded in Orq)

Orq bundles figcraft-server, figcraft-cli and the figcraft web UI (Contents/Resources/figcraft/),
built from figcraft v0.7.0 (https://github.com/storytold/figcraft, commit
47438dd4a2e8b49a7e6bb3dfd480262dadc37f12), dual-licensed under the MIT License or the Apache
License, Version 2.0, at your option.

Changes made by Orq (patches/figcraft/ in the Orq source):
- 0001-orq-branding.patch: the About window and help link point to the upstream repository and
  its licence; third-party product names and links removed.
- 0002-headless-read-poll.patch: headless MCP reads poll the live session first.
- Built with FIGCRAFT_DEFAULT_SERVER empty: no public collaboration server is built in.

The upstream NOTICE, LICENSE-APACHE and LICENSE-MIT are in Contents/Resources/figcraft/licenses/.

Fonts: the binaries and web UI embed fonts from craft-fonts
(https://github.com/storytold/craft-fonts, commit 43913056ce82a3fdad0ef69f6b88d1dc922a8104;
the web UI embeds only Inter), licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Each family's
licence text is in Contents/Resources/figcraft/licenses/OFL-<family>.txt.

Rust crate dependencies keep their own licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, OFL,
CDLA-Permissive-2.0 and similar permissive licenses); see each crate's metadata in figcraft's
Cargo.lock.
